WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.335
Hi, I'm Kerning!

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.425
Ideogram's new model makes SVG files.

00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:07.908
There is no paper, so I opened its sample files.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:13.267
The files read like a picture traced into outlines, with a fitted

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.829
gradient wherever the colour ramps.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.181
Probably, a prompt first becomes a picture.

00:00:23.181 --> 00:00:25.813
Every gallery file shares one square canvas.

00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:29.141
Each colour region is traced and fitted with curves.

00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:32.695
Path starts land on a quarter pixel grid, a tracer's mark.

00:00:33.115 --> 00:00:35.902
A region whose colour ramps gets a gradient of its own.

00:00:36.322 --> 00:00:39.903
Out comes a flat list of filled paths, in the same format

00:00:39.903 --> 00:00:41.097
the image vectorizer writes.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.362
Here is what a single file holds.

00:00:44.782 --> 00:00:46.615
There is no text element anywhere.

00:00:46.615 --> 00:00:48.447
Every letter is a filled outline.

00:00:48.867 --> 00:00:51.306
No groups, no strokes, just shapes back to front.

00:00:51.726 --> 00:00:54.171
A letter's hole is a dark blob painted on top.

00:00:55.775 --> 00:00:59.879
A classical tracer like VTracer has only flat colours, so a smooth

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:01.931
ramp becomes a staircase of bands.

00:01:02.351 --> 00:01:05.655
Ideogram fits a gradient to each ramp, and draws the same lettering

00:01:05.655 --> 00:01:07.306
in a fraction of the shapes.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:14.289
In Ideogram's SVG the letters fade smoothly from cyan to lavender, like the source.

00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:19.061
VTracer's flat layers band the same ramp and leave an outline around each letter.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.494
On that lettering, Ideogram's small file matches the source far more closely.

00:01:25.725 --> 00:01:28.494
So think of it as filled outlines with fitted gradients.

00:01:28.494 --> 00:01:32.095
They scale and stay small, but the type is a drawing of type.

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.583
Letters are outlines.

00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:36.614
Each ramp gets its own gradient.

00:01:36.614 --> 00:01:39.322
And it shares a writer with the vectorizer.

00:01:39.742 --> 00:01:41.913
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.913 --> 00:01:42.533
I'm Kerning.

00:01:42.533 --> 00:01:42.843
Bye!
